# Local CouchDB development configuration
# Copy this file to .env.development (which is gitignored).
# Without it, `yarn dev` runs on the static course (no backend): see README.
#
# Prerequisites (README, "With a backend"):
#   1. A CouchDB on localhost:5984 (admin/password), e.g. the docker one-liner in the README
#   2. Seed the database: yarn --cwd content/phoneticAnalytics db:seed
#   3. Run the app: yarn dev
#
# Setting VITE_COUCH_BASE_URL selects the CouchDB data layer; VITE_DATA_LAYER
# (couch | static) overrides that either way.

VITE_COUCH_BASE_URL=localhost:5984/
VITE_COUCHDB_PROTOCOL=http

# On-device testing (phone/tablet on the same wifi):
#
#   yarn dev:mobile
#
# That detects this machine's LAN address, overrides VITE_COUCH_BASE_URL with
# it, and serves vite on all interfaces — then browse to
# http://<lan-ip>:5173 from the device. Both overrides are needed: 'localhost'
# resolves to the *phone* on the phone, so the default couch URL is
# unreachable there. The dev CSP shim in vite.config.ts derives its allowed
# couch origin from this same variable, so nothing else needs changing.
#
# Note the device is on an insecure origin (plain http, non-localhost), so
# secure-context-only APIs are unavailable — notably navigator.clipboard, which
# makes "copy" buttons silently no-op. Login is unaffected.

# Google sign-in (public). This is our OAuth client, which allows localhost;
# self-hosters need their own. Unset: no Google button.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=586712117502-cerpvh2e1ersf101croapm162cajd0hh.apps.googleusercontent.com
